\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Model Predictive Control (MPC) for Bidirectional DC-DC Converter (Simulink)
\f1\b0\fs32 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 1. Problem: \

\f1\b0 Design and implement a Finite Control Set Model Predictive Control (FCS-MPC) strategy for a Bidirectional DC-DC Converter (e.g., a two-quadrant chopper) used to manage power flow between a 400\'a0V DC bus and a 48\'a0V battery energy storage system (BESS).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 2. Tasks:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl264\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b\fs28 \cf2 Bidirectional Current Tracking:
\f0\i0\fs32  
\f1\b0 Implement a single MPC algorithm that successfully regulates the inductor current (IL) to track a fast-changing reference in both charging (Buck mode) and discharging (Boost mode) directions.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b\fs28 \cf2 Constraint Management
\f3\b0 :
\f1\i0  
\fs32 Incorporate a cost function to minimize the difference between the predicted current and the reference, while simultaneously penalizing overshoots on the inductor current and managing the switching frequency within acceptable limits.\

\f2\i\b\fs28 Real-Time Simulation:
\f1\i0\b0  
\fs32 Model the converter and the MPC algorithm in Simulink/Simscape to demonstrate fast dynamic response, robust mode transition, and stable operation under sudden changes in reference current.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b\fs28 \cf0 Control Comparison:
\f1\i0\b0\fs32  Compare the MPC's transient performance (overshoot, settling time) against a standard \ul Cascaded PI Controlle\ulnone r for the same current reversal test.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

